er-right-width:1pt;border-left-color:#000000;vertical-align:top;border-right-color:#000000;border-left-width:1pt;border-top-style:solid;border-left-style:solid;border-bottom-width:1pt;width:66.9pt;border-top-color:#000000;border-bottom-style:solid"><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Immediate upon Curve Ingestion</span></p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" style="border-right-style:solid;border-bottom-color:#000000;border-top-width:1pt;border-right-width:1pt;border-left-color:#000000;vertical-align:top;border-right-color:#000000;border-left-width:1pt;border-top-style:solid;border-left-style:solid;border-bottom-width:1pt;width:66.9pt;border-top-color:#000000;border-bottom-style:solid"><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Verified OSS Mechanism</span></p></td></tr></tbody></table><h3 style="padding-top:12pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:14pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Architectural Distinction Between APIs</span></h3><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span>The </span><span style="font-weight:700">YouTube Data API v3</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;is authoritative solely for resource discovery, video metadata retrieval, channel configuration, and near-real-time public engagement counters (viewCount, likeCount, commentCount via videos.list?part=statistics). It costs 1 quota unit per call against a 10,000 unit daily project allocation. It provides zero visibility into private metrics such as watch time, retention, impressions, or traffic attribution.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span>The </span><span style="font-weight:700">YouTube Analytics API v2</span><span>&nbsp;provides targeted, dynamic queries over historical metrics with custom dimensional grouping, filtering, and sorting. It operates under a dedicated quota of 10,000 queries per day. Requests require OAuth 2.0 authorization with scopes including https://www.googleapis.com/auth/yt-analytics.readonly and https://www.googleapis.com/auth/yt-analytics-monetary.readonly. Crucially, the Analytics API </span><span style="font-weight:700">does not support reach metrics</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">; requesting videoThumbnailImpressions or videoThumbnailImpressionsClickRate returns an immediate HTTP 400 badRequest error. Its data processing latency is officially documented at 48 to 72 hours, and queries automatically truncate results to the last day where all requested metrics have been fully processed.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span>The </span><span style="font-weight:700">YouTube Reporting API v1</span><span>&nbsp;executes automated bulk data extraction. It does not support interactive queries or ad-hoc filtering. Instead, applications call jobs.create to schedule recurring daily bulk export jobs for predefined report types. YouTube then generates system-managed, gzip-compressed CSV reports on a 24-to-48-hour batch schedule. The Reporting API is the </span><span style="font-weight:700">exclusive programmatic source</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;for reach metrics via the channel_reach_basic_a1 and channel_reach_combined_a1 reports, which expose video_thumbnail_impressions and video_thumbnail_impressions_ctr broken down by date, traffic source, device, and operating system.</span></p><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span>The </span><span style="font-weight:700">YouTube Studio UI</span><span>&nbsp;contains proprietary interfaces such as the 48-hour/60-minute real-time velocity stream and the native "Test &amp; Compare" thumbnail A/B testing tool. As confirmed by developer issue tracking, Test &amp; Compare exposes </span><span style="font-weight:700">zero programmatic API surface</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;in either the Data, Analytics, or Reporting APIs. The engine cannot automate native YouTube Studio A/B test setup or variant result retrieval via official public APIs.</span></p><h2 style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:18pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:18pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">3. Metric Dictionary</span></h2><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Metrics are distinct mathematical representations of platform phenomena, not interchangeable proxies for quality. Conflating diagnostic signals with audience satisfaction leads directly to corrupted production feedback loops.</span></p><table style="border-spacing:0;border-collapse:collapse;margin-right:auto"><thead><tr style="height:0pt"><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" style="border-right-style:solid;border-bottom-color:#000000;border-top-width:1pt;border-right-width:1pt;border-left-color:#000000;vertical-align:top;border-right-color:#000000;border-left-width:1pt;border-top-style:solid;border-left-style:solid;border-bottom-width:1pt;width:66.9pt;border-top-color:#000000;border-bottom-style:solid"><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Metric Name</span></p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" style="border-right-style:solid;border-bottom-color:#000000;border-top-width:1pt;border-right-width:1pt;border-left-color:#000000;vertical-align:top;border-right-color:#000000;border-left-width:1pt;border-top-style:solid;border-left-style:solid;border-bottom-width:1pt;width:66.9pt;border-top-color:#000000;border-bottom-style:solid"><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">API Parameter &amp; Unit</span></p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" style="border-right-style:solid;border-bottom-color:#000000;border-top-width:1pt;border-right-width:1pt;border-left-color:#000000;vertical