d colspan="1" rowspan="1" style="border-right-style:solid;border-bottom-color:#000000;border-top-width:1pt;border-right-width:1pt;border-left-color:#000000;vertical-align:top;border-right-color:#000000;border-left-width:1pt;border-top-style:solid;border-left-style:solid;border-bottom-width:1pt;width:93.6pt;border-top-color:#000000;border-bottom-style:solid"><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Rendered MP4</span></p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" style="border-right-style:solid;border-bottom-color:#000000;border-top-width:1pt;border-right-width:1pt;border-left-color:#000000;vertical-align:top;border-right-color:#000000;border-left-width:1pt;border-top-style:solid;border-left-style:solid;border-bottom-width:1pt;width:93.6pt;border-top-color:#000000;border-bottom-style:solid"><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">QA Verification Report</span></p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" style="border-right-style:solid;border-bottom-color:#000000;border-top-width:1pt;border-right-width:1pt;border-left-color:#000000;vertical-align:top;border-right-color:#000000;border-left-width:1pt;border-top-style:solid;border-left-style:solid;border-bottom-width:1pt;width:93.6pt;border-top-color:#000000;border-bottom-style:solid"><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Loudness compliance (-14 LUFS), black frame count, audio sync</span></p></td></tr></tbody></table><h3 style="padding-top:12pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:14pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Creative Feature Extraction Framework</span></h3><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">To avoid bloated feature spaces, the extraction pipeline isolates fifteen measurable creative characteristics that directly map to script, visual, and audio parameters:</span></p><ol class="lst-kix_list_2-0 start" start="1" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Hook Characteristics</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: Opening duration (seconds to first thematic transition); hook structural type (CURIOSITY_GAP, PROVOCATIVE_CLAIM, DIRECT_QUESTION, IN_MEDIA_RES); narrative setup time (seconds until premise is revealed).</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Script Metrics</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: Total script word count; syntactic density (words per sentence); narration delivery speed (words per minute); scene frequency (scene changes per minute); CTA placement ratio (timestamp of call-to-action divided by total duration).</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Visual Structure</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: Average shot duration (seconds); visual cut frequency (Hz); asset taxonomy distribution (ratio of AI synthetic stills vs 2.5D parallax vs procedural motion graphics vs screen recordings); face presence ratio (percentage of frames containing a primary human or character face); on-screen text overlay ratio.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Audio Architecture</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: Silence ratio (percentage of audio timeline below -45 dBFS); background music presence ratio; music ducking attenuation (decibel separation between speech track and musical bed); narration-to-silence cadence.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Packaging Metadata</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: Title character count; title capitalization ratio; title sentiment polarity score; thumbnail face area ratio; thumbnail text overlay presence (boolean); thumbnail dominant color palette (HSV coordinates).</span></li></ol><h2 style="padding-top:11.2pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:18pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:18pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">7. Audience Retention Analysis and Timeline Mapping</span></h2><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Audience retention curves represent the highest-resolution diagnostic telemetry provided by YouTube. The Analytics API targeted query surfaces this telemetry via the elapsedVideoTimeRatio dimension paired with audienceWatchRatio, returning 100 discrete data points representing percentile buckets (0.01 to 1.00) of total media duration.</span></p><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Courier&quot;;font-style:normal">Targeted Retention Query:<br>ids: channel==MINE<br>dimensions: elapsedVideoTimeRatio<br>metrics: audienceWatchRatio,relativeRetentionPerformance,startedWatch[span_221](start_span)[span_221](end_span)ing,stoppedWatching,totalSegmentImpressions<br>f[span_252](start_span)[span_252](end_span)[span_254](start_span)[span_254](end_span)[span_256](start_span)[span_256](end_span)ilters: video=={VIDEO_ID};audienceType==ORGANIC<br>startDate: {PUBLISH_DATE}<br>endDate: {STABLE_DATE}<br></span></p><h3 style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:14pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Second-by-Second Scene Alignment and Inflection Detection</span></h3><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">To align retention curves with the production timeline, normalized percentiles are projected into physical time coordinates and evaluated using mathematical change-point analysis:</span></p><ol class="lst-kix_list_3-0 start" start="1" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Temporal Projection</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: For each retention bucket i \in [1, 100], the physical timestamp is computed as t_i = \text{elapsedVideoTimeRatio}_i \times \text{duration\_seconds}. The interval width represented by each bucket is \Delta t = \text{duration\_seconds} / 100.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Scene Intersection Mapping</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: The production scene plan defines physical intervals [S_{k,\text{start}}, S_{k,\text{end}}]. The system maps each retention observation t_i to Scene k satisfying S_{k,\text{start}} \le t_i &lt; S_{k,\text{end}}.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Change-Point Detection via PELT</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: Rather than using arbitrary drop thresholds, the Pruned Exact Linear Time (PELT) algorithm from the ruptures library is applied to the sequence of audienceWatchRatio values. PELT solves the penalized optimization problem: \min_{M, \tau} \sum_{m=1}^{M+1} \mathcal{C}(y_{\tau_{m-1}:\tau_m}) + \beta M where \mathcal{C} is the segment cost function (L_2 norm), \tau represents the set of change-point indices, and \beta is the regularization penalty tuned to suppress local noise while capturing structural shifts.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Inflection Classification</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">:</span></li></ol><ul class="lst-kix_list_4-1 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:60pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-style:italic">Intro Drop-off</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: Evaluated strictly over t \in [0, 30\text{s}]. Churn is computed as \Delta_{\text{intro}} = \text{ratio}(t_{30}) - \text{ratio}(t_0). Reflects packaging alignment with initial playback.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:60pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-style:italic">Retention Cliff (Dip)</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: A detected change point where the local gradient d(\text{ratio})/dt &lt; -\theta_{\text{cliff}}, indicating concentrated viewer abandonment.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:60pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-style:italic">Rewatch Spike</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: A segment where d(\text{ratio})/dt &gt; 0 or where local audienceWatchRatio exceeds the rolling average of preceding segments by &gt;2\sigma, identifying backward scrubbing or repeated playback.</span></li></ul><ol class="lst-kix_list_3-0" start="5" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Non-Causal Evidentiary Enforcement</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: The system strictly forbids causal assertions in automated analysis logs.</span></li></ol><ul class="lst-kix_list_5-1 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:60pt;font-family:&quo